<edge source="Investor" target="Securities Company">
  <data key="d8">14.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relationship between an Investor and a Securities Company encompasses a wide range of financial services and interactions. Securities companies offer margin trading and short selling services, where investors can borrow funds or securities to engage in these transactions. Investors open credit securities accounts at these companies, enabling them to participate in margin trading and short selling. The Securities Company also acts as an intermediary, providing securities lending agency services to the Investor.

In addition to trading services, the Securities Company plays a crucial role in fund management and distribution. They provide private fund distribution services, which include opening cash accounts and offering comprehensive information. Investors submit fund purchase applications along with their identity documents to the Securities Company, and they can also submit redemption applications when needed. The company issues yield certificates and provides various financial services to both individual and institutional investors. 

Securities companies manage the fund investment portfolios for investors, regularly communicating with them to understand their needs and adjust investment strategies accordingly. They also provide research services, helping investors to understand market trends and receive investment advice. For one-time financial services, such as bond subscription and allocation, the Securities Company handles the process and ensures that the investor's requirements are met. 

Furthermore, the Securities Company offers single asset management services, often formalized through an Asset Management Contract. This service includes ensuring the safety of the fund's assets and providing regular reports to both the Fund Manager and the Investor. These comprehensive services aim to support investors in making informed decisions and managing their financial assets effectively.</data>
  <data key="d10">account management,account opening,agency,application submission,bond subscription,communication,confirmation,contract signing,financial service,financial services,financial transaction,fund purchase,fund safety,investor,issuer,market analysis,notification,one-time transaction,portfolio management,redemption,reporting,research service,service provision</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eca88e9c19c1f56a5fea30694315e711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f911bfae3277fd2e4d6cbb22022ad159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee3b0210e973d3725a10ad55081dd7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce36971547dce4e14d361ad14139277e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f07b36f52ee4a9ce5b004be2a76b530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9faa4149e4811536fbaa26f4404f24d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be4853d73f55dbee5a39e138f9738079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec18b664ecf3e882043bc0024559c17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a847dfe2775f29788ef106c84c01b8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d12e280833046d066b7aaf24d66d3be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1caa07f33ec0d99521d1f30e6329987c</data>
  <data key="d12">1.5证券业精细化洗钱风险管控体系建设研究报告.docx</data>
  <data key="d13">1780068945</data>
