<edge source="Stock Exchange" target="Securities Company">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Securities companies use stock exchanges to conduct and confirm stock pledge repurchase transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Securities companies use stock exchanges to execute authorized fund transactions, such as buying closed-end funds and ETFs.&lt;SEP&gt;The securities company submits application documents, such as the prospectus and financial statements, to the stock exchange for detailed review.&lt;SEP&gt;Securities Company conducts transactions through the Stock Exchange and follows its rules and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Stock exchanges provide the necessary trading venues and facilities for securities companies to conduct bond transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Stock Exchange provides a platform for Securities Company to execute public fund transactions, match trades, and send transaction data for verification and settlement.</data>
