<edge source="Securities Company" target="Fund Manager">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The fund manager and the securities company are both involved in managing and overseeing the public fund products, with the securities company needing to detect and prevent fraudulent activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Securities Company processes the Investor's redemption application and forwards it to the Fund Manager, who then transfers the redemption funds back to the Securities Company.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fund Manager transfers the redemption funds to the Securities Company, which then transfers the funds to the Investor's account.&lt;SEP&gt;The Securities Company signs a custody agreement with the Fund Manager and supervises the fund's operations, including investment transactions and fund valuations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fund Manager outsources fund operation services to the Securities Company through a formal agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fund Manager signs a service agreement with the Securities Company to obtain trading and settlement services for the Public Fund.</data>
  <data key="d10">agreement,fraud detection,fund transfer,outsourcing,redemption,redemption processing,regulatory oversight,service agreement,service provision,settlement,supervision,trade execution</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-eca88e9c19c1f56a5fea30694315e711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce36971547dce4e14d361ad14139277e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f12cdeb483c7deb72fe0b6a5c6a479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908a90bfb004325d95720427d14fe150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc40bbb1d762462c190a313215ef8a3c</data>
